          "0": {
            "id": "14083489",
            "headline": "Live: Capital market stocks hit on Sebi's MTF rules report, Metal stocks slide | Closing Bell",
            "heading": "Live: Capital market stocks hit on Sebi's MTF rules report, Metal stocks slide | Closing Bell",
            "slug": "live-capital-market-stocks-hit-on-sebi-s-mtf-rules-report-metal-stocks-slide-closing-bell",
            "intro": "Indian equity benchmarks retreated on Wednesday, a day after touching 9-month highs, with the Sensex slipping over 300 points and the Nifty sliding below the 25,300 mark as declines outpaced advances. Capital market stocks came under pressure following a report on Sebi\u2019s proposed MTF rules, while metal and consumer durable stocks were among the worst hit and midcaps saw a sell-off. Pharma and PSU banking stocks bucked the weak trend, with Cipla, SBI and Apollo Hospitals leading the Nifty 50 gainers, while Titan, HDFC Life and Hindalco were the top losers. Globally, Brent crude hovered around $91 per barrel, the Kospi rebounded on Nvidia\u2019s strong results, and US futures traded in the green after Tuesday\u2019s sell-off. Watch the full Closing Bell show for the complete breakdown of the day\u2019s market action, sectoral trends and key stocks in focus.",
