          "2": {
            "id": "14083414",
            "headline": "Subscribe for Mahanadi Coalfields Ltd IPO; Prabhudas Lilladher",
            "heading": "Subscribe for Mahanadi Coalfields Ltd IPO; Prabhudas Lilladher",
            "intro": "Prabhudas Lilladher, has come out with its report on Mahanadi Coalfields Ltd The research firm has recommended to \u201c Subscribe\u201d the ipo in its research report as on November 17, 2026.",
            "body": "Prabhudas Lilladher, Mahanadi Coalfields Ltd\r\nMahanadi Coalfields (MCL), a wholly owned subsidiary of Coal India (COAL), is coming out with an IPO. The IPO is entirely an OFS, with Coal India planning to dilute its 10% stake while retaining 90% ownership. MCL contributed 28% to COAL\u2019s coal dispatch and 33% to its EBITDA in FY26. MCL follows a relatively focused capital allocation strategy, with investments largely directed toward mine development and coalfield expansion. Investments in unrelated businesses such as fertilizers and thermal power, are undertaken at the holding company (Coal India) level. MCL reported EBITDA margin of ~42% compared with ~22% (FY26) for Coal India. This could be partly attributed to: 1) MCL\u2019s favorable strip ratio of ~1.0x, resulting in relatively lower overburden removal requirements and mining costs, and 2) employee cost being 15% of its revenue versus 28% of COAL. MCL\u2019s RoE of ~50% is significantly higher than Coal India\u2019s 30% (FY26), supported by superior operating margins and better asset turnover, reflecting stronger asset utilization and capital efficiency. At the IPO price, MCL offers a trailing dividend yield of ~8.5%, compared with ~6.6% for Coal India (FY26), making it attractive from a cash-return perspective.\r\n&amp;nbsp;\r\nValuation and Outlook\r\nAt the proposed IPO market capitalization of ~INR900bn, MCL is valued at 10-15% premium to Coal India\u2019s ~5x (FY26). The modest premium appears justified by MCL\u2019s superior operating profitability (EBITDA CAGR over FY20- 26 at 6% vs CIL at 5%) and return ratios, and focused capital allocation. We recommend subscribe for mid to long term.\r\nFor all\u00a0IPO report,\u00a0click here\r\nDisclaimer:\u00a0The views and investment tips expressed by investment experts/broking houses/rating agencies on moneycontrol.com are their own, and not that of the website or its management. Moneycontrol.com advises users to check with certified experts before taking any investment decisions.\r\nMahanadi Coalfields -181126 - prabhu",
